// N0 corpus row `call-arg-overlap` (plans/backlog/REFERENCES_AND_ORIGINS.md §8 N0;
// manifest tests/origins/corpus.tsv): a `&` relend of a place an earlier argument of the same call lends `&mut` (O3 step 2 / decision 28 restated).
// Expected once decision 43's rules land: rejected: E0910. Rejected E0910 today too since B8 made `ArrayList` a value (decision 28's value-root rule); before B8 the list was a reference type and the `&` relend passed.
{ ArrayList } :: import("std/collections/array_list");
_both :: (fn(a : &mut ArrayList(i32), b : &ArrayList(i32)) -> unit)(a.push(i32(b.len())));
main :: (fn() -> unit)({
  mut(xs) := ArrayList(i32).new();
  _both(&mut xs, &xs);
  ()
});
export(main);
